CORE
JmlAggregate
--function JmlAggregate.sumGE --jml-source src/main/java/JmlAggregate.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for JML \sum aggregate expansion with transposed
bounds (REVIEW-PRE-PUSH high item 5).

Pre-fix: jml_lowering.cpp's bound-matching code lumped LE and
GE into the same branch and conflated `var <= lb` with
`lb <= var`. As a result, range conditions like `i >= 0 && i <= 4`
would mis-classify the bounds (treating an upper bound as a
lower bound), producing wrong expansion or no expansion at all.

Post-fix: bound matching canonicalises by checking which side
contains the bound variable; conjuncts are flipped to `var <op'> k`
form before classification.

This test exercises the GE form (`i >= 0 && i <= 4`); the
sum-from-0-to-4 = 10 and matches the LT form
`0 <= i && i < 5; i` which is verified by sumLT in the same file.
